{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.47448267673864636, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No integrity problems. The diff only adds parse(), which keeps the largest fragment (salt stripping) and is used in all three featurizers. It reads no files, pastes no answers and never touches the test labels.", "Minor robustness point, not a veto: if a SMILES string fails to parse, parse() silently swaps in benzene. This hides parse failures instead of reporting them. The original code would have crashed on None, so this is not a bug that makes the score meaningless.", "The candidate's 0.4745 is exactly equal to the incumbent's. This suggests either that almost no molecules in the dataset contain multiple fragments, or that removing counter-ions does not change the features in a way that matters. The change has no measurable effect.", "Recomputed z: (0.4745 - 0.4745) / (0.0070 * sqrt(1/1 + 1/1)) = 0.000. This agrees with the harness. Rejecting is consistent with the numbers. If the team prefers simpler code, the extra code is not justified by any gain, though salt stripping is a reasonable default for the final model trained on all the data."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Route all three featurizers through a parse() helper that keeps only the largest fragment (by heavy atoms) of each SMILES, so salts and counterions no longer distort descriptors, ErG, or Morgan counts.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "walnut", "idea_id": "b016", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.47448267673864636, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.47448267673864636, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B2_clear_SS_2_s1-candidate-7_1795071447974", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.00211704, "cost_usd_plan": 0.00211704, "latency_s": 8.18918763200054, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "coder", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 7511, "tokens_out": 1756}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0245118,