{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.47891165226840615, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No way around the measurement found. The Ridge model is fit only on the training features and train labels. Test molecules are only passed to predict(). No file or network access, and no pasted values.", "No bug that would make the result meaningless. The edit only changes the Ridge alpha (10 to 3) and the blend weights (0.7/0.3 to 0.6/0.4). Both parts are rank-normalized and the weights still add up to 1.", "The numbers check out. The candidate's loss of 0.4789 is 0.0044 worse than the incumbent's 0.4745. With noise sd 0.0070 and one run on each side, z = -0.0044/(0.0070*sqrt(2)) \u2248 -0.44, which matches the reported -0.445 (the sign convention is negative = worse). This is well within noise, so rejecting is reasonable.", "Note: with only one run on each side, this comparison can't tell small differences apart."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Change the Ridge member to alpha=3.0 and raise its blend weight from 0.3 to 0.4 (rank-average weight 0.6), with nothing else changed.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "walnut", "idea_id": "b032", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.47448267673864636, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.47448267673864636, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B2_clear_SS_2_s1-candidate-15_1795073260774", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.00157594, "cost_usd_plan": 0.00157594, "latency_s": 4.217605744022876, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "coder", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 7268, "tokens_out": 771}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.021559799999999997, "cost_usd_plan": 0.021559799999999997, "latency_s": 7.055168804014102, "requested_model": "opus", "role": "critic", "served_model": "opus", "tokens_in": 2525, "tokens_out": 614}], "official_val_bpb": 0.47891165226840615, "sealed_val_bpb": null, "slot": 15, "status": "ok", "ts": "2026-11-